<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mao Zedong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1893">1893</a>–<a href="/years/1976">1976</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Chairman Mao</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mao Zedong was a founding member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-communist-party">Chinese Communist Party</a> who led the Chinese Soviet Republic in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangxi">Jiangxi</a> and emerged as party leader during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/long-march">Long March</a> of 1934–1935. After victory in the civil war he proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a> in 1949 and ruled it until his death. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-leap-forward">Great Leap Forward</a> caused a famine that killed tens of millions, and he launched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cultural-revolution">Cultural Revolution</a> in 1966.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mao-zedong.jpg" alt="Mao Zedong" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chen Zhengqing (1917–1966) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mao_Zedong_1950_Portrait_(3x4_cropped)(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…Kuomintang collapsed in 1927, the party built rural base areas, proclaimed the Chinese Soviet Republic in Jiangxi in 1931 and, driven out by Nationalist encirclement campaigns, made the Long March of 1934–35 to northern Shaanxi, where Yan’an became its base, during which <b>Mao Zedong</b> rose to the leadership.</blockquote><a href="/empire/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1939 <b>Mao Zedong</b> called it a new stage in China’s bourgeois-democratic revolution against imperialism and feudalism, a step beyond the Revolution of 1911, and the historian Wang Gungwu notes that it came to be seen as the predecessor of the Cultural Revolution.</blockquote><a href="/movement/may-fourth-movement">May Fourth Movement · Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote>The Taiping mix of Christianity and radical social equality influenced Sun Yat-sen, and Chinese Communist historians, following <b>Mao Zedong</b>, called the rising proto-communist; John King Fairbank compared the Taiping with Mao’s communists.</blockquote><a href="/movement/taiping-rebellion">Taiping Rebellion · Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote>After Nazi Germany’s defeat in 1945 the Soviet Union imposed communist dictatorships across Central and Eastern Europe, and in 1949 <b>Mao Zedong</b> proclaimed the People’s Republic of China.</blockquote><a href="/government/dictatorship">Dictatorship · Through History</a></li><li><blockquote>Trade unions, youth leagues and women’s organisations serve as “transmission belts” between party and people, and the armed forces answer to the party; in <b>Mao Zedong</b>’s words, “the party commands the gun”.</blockquote><a href="/government/one-party-state">One-party state · How It Works</a></li><li><blockquote>The English word Maoism was coined in 1951 by Benjamin I. Schwartz; Mao himself avoided it and preferred <b>Mao Zedong</b> Thought, since he saw his ideas as still developing rather than a complete system.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/maoism">Maoism · At a glance</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Shaoshan, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. Died in Zhongnanhai, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=27.91,112.48&amp;year=1946" aria-label="Shaoshan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7499 1141 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Mao Zedong"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7949 1411h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7949 1411h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=27.91,112.48&amp;year=1946">What was here in 1946? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
